{"connection_id": "BC-694c8528c714c0749a13", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.6.7", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lawsuits already a defeat", "note": "The commentary's human being is in loss until a shared ethic replaces contention; Paul calls lawsuits among believers already a defeat and asks why they do not bear wrong."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4f2c75b356ddd0ee4973", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.6.8", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wrong and defraud brothers", "note": "The commentary's claimed right can become injury to the other side; Paul says the litigating Corinthians themselves wrong and defraud their own brothers, reversing the ethic of mutual benefit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4bbe946307f9402a5ecd", "ref": "SBLGNT:1John.1.7", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "walking in light yields fellowship with one another", "note": "The letter joins shared truthfulness before God to fellowship among believers; this connects the commentary's haqq with its movement toward closeness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f200070e18e1fac67d60", "ref": "SBLGNT:1John.3.14", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "love of brothers and escape from death", "note": "The commentary contrasts the human in loss with believers joined by affection; John says love for brothers marks a passage from death to life."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9f5765ded3cbfbab29cb", "ref": "SBLGNT:1John.3.16", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "give life for brothers", "note": "The commentary's close friendship issues in righteous action; John says Christ's laying down his life teaches believers to lay down their lives for brothers."}
{"connection_id": "BC-767ceba15bf8aaaf5243", "ref": "SBLGNT:1John.3.17", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "material care for needy brother", "note": "The commentary invokes the failure to encourage food for the poor; John asks how God's love can remain in one who sees a needy brother and shuts up compassion."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5b9e658c7876bebde582", "ref": "SBLGNT:1John.3.18", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "love in deed and truth", "note": "The commentary's joined good deeds and shared haqq require action; John tells the community to love in deed and truth, not merely in speech."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e7f66832c51ba70d5d59", "ref": "SBLGNT:1John.4.20", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "claiming love for God while hating a brother is false", "note": "The letter tests religious claim against treatment of the visible brother; this challenges any haqq claim detached from mutual care."}
