{"connection_id": "BC-6d2162a2b2449a07dadd", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.13.11", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "restore, encourage, agree, and live in peace", "note": "Paul joins restoration and mutual encouragement to agreement and peace, closely matching the commentary's sequence from conflict to togetherness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3d5595483d886ee5db50", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.2.7", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "forgive and comfort the offender", "note": "The commentary's peace removes fearful estrangement; Paul urges the community to forgive and comfort a punished person so excessive sorrow does not overwhelm him."}
{"connection_id": "BC-395e353dbc607180dfc5", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.2.8", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "reaffirm love after discipline", "note": "The commentary turns disagreement toward an enduring bond; Paul asks the community to confirm its love for the person it disciplined, making affection an explicit act of restoration."}
