{"connection_id": "BC-95c6a74c810059cc463f", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.3.8", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "unity, sympathy, brotherly love, and humility", "note": "Peter places one-mindedness and brotherly compassion together; this gives the commentary's move from estrangement to intimacy a compact communal ethic."}
{"connection_id": "BC-90916dcc9c688963b6da", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.3.8", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "unity and brotherly love", "note": "The commentary develops closeness from estrangement; Peter asks all to have unity of mind, sympathy, brotherly love and humility."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c30d8ac9cdf17e240c5c", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.3.9", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "answer hostility with blessing", "note": "The commentary's enemy-to-friend turn requires patience; Peter forbids returning evil or reviling in kind and commands blessing instead."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6371e659c181db7b2725", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.4.8", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "love covers many sins", "note": "Peter says sustained love covers many sins; this fits the commentary's transition from contention toward a bond that can absorb offense."}
{"connection_id": "BC-22d950337ec5839ef499", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.4.8", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "love covers many sins", "note": "The commentary's patience permits estranged companions to stay together; Peter urges sustained love for one another because love covers a multitude of sins."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1c3fdd2fe3c77f09c85d", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.4.9", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hospitality without grumbling", "note": "The commentary's reciprocal care keeps others close; Peter asks members to show hospitality to one another without complaint, giving affectionate attachment a household practice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-dafe83ae4073bf4f8b87", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.11", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "encourage and build each other", "note": "The commentary's mutual action makes the community stronger; Paul tells believers to encourage and build one another, noting that they already do so."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fc146cbb75b41a7f1631", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.14", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "admonish, encourage, help, and be patient with all", "note": "The community is to give different forms of support to the idle, fainthearted, and weak, then remain patient with everyone; this is reciprocal counsel enacted as care."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a03657d158064158a0b9", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.14", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "patient help within the group", "note": "The commentary's companion stands with others in patience; Paul assigns differentiated mutual duties to admonish the idle, encourage the fainthearted, help the weak and be patient with all."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a5596daa3af4c5437696", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Thess.5.15", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "seek good for one another", "note": "The commentary's mutual action replaces retaliation; Paul forbids repaying evil for evil and directs believers always to seek good for one another and everyone."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6d2162a2b2449a07dadd", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.13.11", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "restore, encourage, agree, and live in peace", "note": "Paul joins restoration and mutual encouragement to agreement and peace, closely matching the commentary's sequence from conflict to togetherness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3d5595483d886ee5db50", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.2.7", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "forgive and comfort the offender", "note": "The commentary's peace removes fearful estrangement; Paul urges the community to forgive and comfort a punished person so excessive sorrow does not overwhelm him."}
{"connection_id": "BC-395e353dbc607180dfc5", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.2.8", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "reaffirm love after discipline", "note": "The commentary turns disagreement toward an enduring bond; Paul asks the community to confirm its love for the person it disciplined, making affection an explicit act of restoration."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c78bf48daa57440514c0", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Thess.3.15", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "admonish as brother, not enemy", "note": "The commentary transforms the opponent into a companion through counsel; Paul says the disobedient member is to be admonished as a brother rather than regarded as an enemy."}
{"connection_id": "BC-32ede8a4f0b8dc82649a", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.2.23", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "foolish disputes breed quarrels", "note": "The commentary's opening rivals fight over what they call right; this instruction says foolish and ignorant controversies produce quarrels, supplying a diagnosis of failed counsel."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6b1f7e4e9c5eae576fc3", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.2.24", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the Lord's servant must not quarrel but be patient", "note": "The teacher is to avoid strife, remain gentle, and endure patiently; this directly links sabr to how one handles opponents."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ddd76771178f3e344164", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.2.24", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's servant avoids quarrels", "note": "The commentary reverses rival claims into patient counsel; this instruction says the Lord's servant must not quarrel but be kind to everyone and able to teach."}
{"connection_id": "BC-08d66d5ebfd7ea10617e", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.2.25", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "correct opponents with gentleness", "note": "Correction is to be offered gently even to those who oppose; this gives mutual counsel a manner aimed at restoration rather than victory."}
{"connection_id": "BC-07985eac141fd2b03308", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Tim.2.25", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "gentle correction of opponents", "note": "The commentary's truth is conveyed to the other side instead of used for contention; the servant corrects opponents with gentleness in hope of their turning toward truth."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5ea140dd58e76ca31801", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.15.2", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "dispute and debate over circumcision", "note": "The believers' serious dispute over Gentile inclusion gives the commentary's contested claims a concrete communal case rather than a generic quarrel."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8217995db74e77a13f6d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.15.28", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "communal decision reached with the Spirit and the assembly", "note": "The council says its decision seemed good to the Holy Spirit and to them together; this gives the preceding dispute a shared, non-solitary resolution."}
{"connection_id": "BC-986a29ad311cc013a9f1", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.15.39", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "sharp dispute separates coworkers", "note": "The commentary moves contention toward companionship; Paul and Barnabas instead have a sharp disagreement and separate, showing that fellow believers' dispute can remain unresolved in the narrated moment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-34ac00d57b93a61407b4", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.4.32", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "one heart and soul with possessions shared", "note": "The believers hold themselves as one community and treat possessions as common; this gives the commentary's people-joining image a material practice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-66fedd1c1175b15f36be", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.4.32", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "believers one heart and soul", "note": "The commentary moves from the lone human to a mutually sustaining believing group; Acts depicts the multitude of believers as one heart and soul, with no private claim to possessions."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d625fd9518cc7dd383ef", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.6.1", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "widows neglected amid group division", "note": "The commentary cites neglect of the needy as failure of shared obligation; Acts reports a complaint of Hellenists against Hebrews because their widows were overlooked in daily distribution."}
{"connection_id": "BC-46075658394ca3cc36ef", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.9.27", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Barnabas introduces feared Saul to the apostles", "note": "When the disciples fear Saul, Barnabas stands with him and vouches for his changed life; an intermediary turns aversion into acceptance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f81950c792bd4311d935", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.3.13", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bear with and forgive one another", "note": "The instruction makes forbearance and forgiveness reciprocal; it shows patience operating directly between people."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2d42febd8ebc953bb86d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.3.13", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bear and forgive each other", "note": "The commentary's sabr supports reconciliation where people have complaints; Paul tells believers to bear with and forgive one another when a complaint arises."}
{"connection_id": "BC-36435868d6249a49856a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.3.14", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "love binds everything together", "note": "Love is named the bond that brings the virtues to completion; this adds a binding image to the commentary's account of people joining one another."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3ff0941336793076a3d1", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.3.14", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "love as bond", "note": "The commentary names affection and kinship as a bond whose absence marks distance; Paul calls love the bond that completes the virtues."}
{"connection_id": "BC-67c504eb566e4597b2f8", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.3.15", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "peace of Christ rules in one body", "note": "The one body is to be governed by peace; this links reconciliation with the communal unity developed in the commentary."}
{"connection_id": "BC-458df4fcd09387deb09a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.3.15", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "peace governs one body", "note": "The commentary's separated people become a connected believing group; Paul says Christ's peace should rule in their hearts because they were called in one body."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fbedc249b4a034bdfcde", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.3.16", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "teach and admonish one another", "note": "The commentary's repeated reciprocal verb makes each a giver and receiver of counsel; Paul says the word should dwell richly in the community as members teach and admonish one another."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fc1c7a01fd7c5d77fe0d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.14", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Christ makes two groups one by breaking hostility", "note": "The letter pictures peace as removing the dividing wall between groups; this gives the commentary's sulh a concrete image of estrangement dismantled."}
{"connection_id": "BC-347d0c5417031e551aad", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.14", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hostility barrier broken", "note": "The commentary depicts enemies becoming close; Christ makes two groups one and breaks their dividing wall of hostility, an explicit transformation of social distance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e303d7e15284aff7dcf2", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.16", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "reconciliation in one body", "note": "The commentary's hostile sides become a joined group; Paul describes reconciling both groups to God in one body through the cross and killing the hostility."}
{"connection_id": "BC-15312f24745896d58a66", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.15", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "truth spoken in love grows the body", "note": "The letter links truth-telling to love and the growth of the whole body; this adds a communal result to the commentary's exchange of haqq."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d129b3a3779eb230e890", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.15", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "truth spoken in love", "note": "The commentary's haqq is shared within recovered affection; speaking truth in love builds growth into Christ, making the manner of transmission part of the truth's work."}

item.stdout:
{"connection_id": "BC-3a7a1b612b48f2ca62b2", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.2", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "patience bears with one another in love", "note": "The community is told to practice humility, patience, and forbearance toward one another; this connects the commentary's ṣabr to sustaining relationship."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e34a039eeb791beced64", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.2", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "patience bearing one another in love", "note": "The commentary links patience to standing beside a companion; Paul joins patience, humility and bearing with one another in love as the practice of shared life."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2ea7d1929fe4d768b86b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.25", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "speak truth to neighbor because members belong to one another", "note": "Paul joins truthful speech to mutual membership in one body; this directly links the commentary's haqq with its hand-to-hand relation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c923d72cf8366909f009", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.25", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "truth to neighbor because members of each other", "note": "The commentary insists each participant gives and receives truth; Paul commands truthful speech to one's neighbor because believers are members of one another."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4c153fb6d6327ec01815", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.29", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "speech that builds the other up", "note": "The commentary's mutual exhortation gives another person what is needed; Paul asks for speech suited to building up hearers and giving them grace, rather than harmful talk."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a91ab7121fee3aa86550", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.3", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "unity held by the bond of peace", "note": "The letter describes peace as the bond that preserves communal unity; this closely meets the commentary's movement from aversion to attachment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f71faf717941fd2edb46", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.3", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "unity in bond of peace", "note": "The commentary's separated people are joined again; Paul asks believers to maintain the Spirit's unity in the bond of peace, turning attachment into a sustained task."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4035440db8ac7ff3dae7", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.4.32", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "kindness and reciprocal forgiveness", "note": "The commentary says peace removes estrangement; Paul asks members to be kind and tenderhearted, forgiving one another as God forgave them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cdf3fca45a9a0e22d2bb", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.2.12", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "fear causes withdrawal from fellowship", "note": "The commentary says peace removes frightened separation; Peter withdraws from eating with Gentiles because he fears the circumcision group, a concrete reverse of shared company."}
{"connection_id": "BC-88447b31511cf9898041", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.2.14", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "truth requires public correction", "note": "The commentary turns contest over haqq into truth shared for the community's good; Paul challenges Peter's withdrawal publicly because it contradicts the truth of the gospel."}
{"connection_id": "BC-41e3be67d6af9b69d7ac", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.5.13", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "serve one another through love", "note": "The commentary changes mutual action from dispute into affectionate service; Paul commands believers to use freedom to serve one another through love."}
{"connection_id": "BC-239f07a5063a7fe5b349", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.5.15", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "mutual hostility consumes the group", "note": "The commentary says contention weakens a community; Paul warns that biting and devouring one another can end with the disputants consumed by each other."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b1bf2ab074e5935ec9ec", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.1", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "restore the transgressor gently", "note": "Paul says to restore a caught person in a spirit of gentleness while watching oneself; correction becomes mutual care rather than adversarial judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1058b0ac4fb54c2d909b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.1", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "gentle restoration of a member", "note": "The commentary makes counsel a patient act for a companion's good; Paul directs spiritual members to restore someone caught in a transgression gently while watching their own vulnerability."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c88dc67e7f6c3118f1e4", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.2", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bear one another's burdens", "note": "The command to carry one another's burdens makes the commentary's move from the solitary human to companions who stand together concrete."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7093ad4b6c30e3529138", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.6.2", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bear one another's burdens", "note": "The commentary's members give and receive aid; Paul tells them to bear each other's burdens, turning companionship into a concrete shared action."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9c7eb61d315813d1f799", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.24", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "consider one another and stir up love and good works", "note": "The letter makes attention to others the source of mutual encouragement toward good deeds, closely joining the commentary's work and reciprocal advice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bfef531d1b424618cda9", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.24", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "spur one another to love and good works", "note": "The commentary joins mutual urging to righteous deeds and affection; Hebrews asks believers to consider how to stir each other toward love and good works."}
{"connection_id": "BC-01f9e8d978c8910d33d2", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.25", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "encourage one another as the day approaches", "note": "The command to encourage each other makes perseverance communal, matching the commentary's counsel of patience passed between people."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8ab1e36f82636ca5c7e3", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.10.25", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "encourage one another in assembly", "note": "The commentary joins companions who might separate; Hebrews contrasts neglect of meeting together with mutual encouragement as the day approaches."}
{"connection_id": "BC-84407c0615620334ebd7", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.12.14", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "pursue peace with everyone", "note": "The commentary presents peace as an active repair of alienation; Hebrews commands pursuing peace with all, alongside holiness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b9da35d4e95d4231f402", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.12.15", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bitterness troubles many", "note": "The commentary's link between people can be broken by a growing quarrel; Hebrews warns that a bitter root can spring up, cause trouble and defile many."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a8d57a28b43ce0fd2f75", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.3.13", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "exhort one another daily", "note": "The commentary highlights mutual exhortation as the way out of loss; Hebrews commands daily mutual exhortation so no one is hardened by deceitful sin."}
{"connection_id": "BC-493d591e3f3e998c9e00", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.1.19", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hear first and restrain anger", "note": "The commentary's reciprocal counsel requires receiving the other's word and patient speech; James commands quick hearing, slow speaking and slow anger."}
{"connection_id": "BC-098c9b1a1c05d6d3a10e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.2.15", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "brother or sister lacks food and clothes", "note": "The commentary cites failure to urge food for the poor as a breach of mutual obligation; James places a needy brother or sister without daily food before the speaking community."}
{"connection_id": "BC-75dcc9f8b7e1c022a051", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.2.16", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "go in peace without giving food", "note": "The commentary insists on good deeds beside faith and on real care for the needy; James depicts someone wishing a needy person peace but withholding bodily necessities, exposing empty peaceful speech."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fbe2c8b01fc1e00dd4d1", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.3.16", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "jealous rivalry disorders community", "note": "The commentary cites quarrel as loss of collective strength; James says jealousy and selfish ambition bring disorder and every vile practice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e985abd0b74b673a1eb6", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.3.17", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wisdom gentle and peaceable", "note": "The commentary's truth is passed without quarrel; James describes wisdom from above as peaceable, gentle and open to reason, an ethical mode for exchanging counsel."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1678b89bd0bc50187eee", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.3.18", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "righteousness is sown in peace by peacemakers", "note": "James makes peace the soil and peacemakers the agents of a harvest of righteousness; this directly joins the commentary's haqq and sulh."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1f3b73c9e832a11120a1", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.3.18", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "righteousness sown in peace", "note": "The commentary joins righteous works to the ending of quarrel; James says a harvest of righteousness is sown in peace by peacemakers."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4d5ca52719d062357f6b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.4.1", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "quarrels arise within the community", "note": "The commentary begins with two sides contesting right; James asks where their wars and fights come from and locates them in desires at war within them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c38e56caeacdd5fc9dc6", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.5.16", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "confess and pray for one another", "note": "The commentary's reciprocal counsel includes receiving help; James commands mutual confession and prayer so members may be healed, joining truthful disclosure to reciprocal care."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0c21fdc6de4af4032cb5", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.5.19", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "turn a person wandering from truth", "note": "The commentary's counsel is something believers do for one another; James envisages one member bringing back another who has wandered from the truth."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9a89ce8d7ab27eafdd1b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.5.20", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "recover a sinner from error", "note": "The commentary's mutual counsel averts loss; James says turning a sinner back from error saves that person's soul from death."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c1f0d75d3d25bcdebeaf", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.13.34", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "mutual love commanded", "note": "The commentary's members advise and sustain each other in affection; Jesus commands disciples to love one another as he has loved them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-70abfd5ab92feff9702a", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.13.35", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "mutual love identifies disciples", "note": "The commentary's reciprocal bond defines the believing group; Jesus says others will recognize his disciples by their love for one another."}
