{"connection_id": "BC-271e0e1d3b0e60a4d12b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.17.3", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "rebuke a brother who sins", "note": "Jesus commands attention to a brother's wrongdoing; with the following forgiveness instruction, correction serves the relationship rather than a contest over right."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3a0c846969f1eeffc522", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.17.3", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "rebuke and forgive a brother", "note": "The commentary joins truthful counsel with repaired kinship; Jesus directs a disciple to rebuke a sinning brother and forgive him on repentance, giving both actions their place."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d04bdcea774e58c863cd", "ref": "SBLGNT:Luke.17.4", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "forgive a repentant brother repeatedly", "note": "Jesus says to forgive the same brother even after repeated offenses if he repents; this makes patience a repeated practice sustaining kinship."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6c8808ca1878adca803a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Mark.9.50", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "be at peace with one another after rivalry", "note": "After the disciples argue over greatness and dispute who belongs with them, Jesus tells them to have salt and be at peace with one another; the instruction answers internal rivalry directly."}
{"connection_id": "BC-882ef7ef5f1fa2df2702", "ref": "SBLGNT:Mark.9.50", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "be at peace with one another", "note": "The commentary ends with reciprocal action among believers; Jesus explicitly tells his disciples to have peace with one another after their dispute about rank."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3a70c53d877a61443967", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.12.25", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "division destroys collective strength", "note": "The commentary cites quarrelling as the cause of a group's weakened force; Jesus says a kingdom divided against itself is laid waste and a divided city or house will not stand."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bf45fcaaadc0c97868d1", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.18.15", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "private correction aims to regain a brother", "note": "The offended person is to speak directly and, if heard, has gained a brother; this makes admonition a means of restoring kinship rather than winning a case."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5acfcad58a37ca1e68de", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.18.15", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "private correction of brother", "note": "The commentary makes truth something passed to the other person rather than fought over; Jesus tells one to confront a sinning brother privately with the aim of gaining him."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f1f9c458c5518da939f0", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.18.19", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "two agree together in prayer", "note": "The commentary's reciprocal action draws separated members into concord; Jesus says two who agree on earth about a request will be heard by the Father, within his teaching on community disputes."}
