{"connection_id": "BC-646bfa88cd453d47bfe6", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.18.22", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "forgive a brother repeatedly", "note": "Jesus tells Peter to forgive not a few times but repeatedly; this extends the commentary's patience into sustained repair after recurring offense."}
{"connection_id": "BC-93f7a6e8be91b2823940", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.18.22", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "repeated forgiveness", "note": "The commentary's patience sustains restored ties; Jesus' answer to Peter rejects a small limit on forgiving a brother, extending reconciliation beyond a single settlement."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cce6982415bd97660169", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.18.35", "target": "sec9", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "forgive brother from the heart", "note": "The commentary's peace must heal the bond beneath formal settlement; Jesus closes the unforgiving servant story by requiring forgiveness of one's brother from the heart."}
