+{"connection_id":"BC-14b0b864d69c96838cb3","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.1.10","status":"rejected","reason":"Paul asks for common speech and no divisions, but the verse does not show rival right claims being adjudicated; 1 Cor 6:6-7 provides that closer scene.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.1.10"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-8c739fae978e92021917","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.1.11","status":"rejected","reason":"Chloe's report merely establishes quarrels; the selected 1 Cor 6:6-7 specifies litigation and loss, the paragraph's distinctive movement.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.1.11"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-25a6d0cc1be7024f45b0","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.11.21","status":"rejected","reason":"The hungry and drunk at the Lord's supper concern unequal meal practice; paragraph 27 mentions poor feeding only as a Qur'anic analogy to mutual urging, not a meal scene.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.11.21"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c5e4628fcb9d03e8b712","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.11.22","status":"rejected","reason":"Shaming those with nothing is a real meal injustice but gives no further account of reciprocal truth or reconciliation beyond 11:21.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.11.22"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-dd891d95dab06453d1ce","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.11.33","status":"rejected","reason":"Waiting for one another repairs a specific supper abuse, while this section's mutual verb concerns truth and endurance rather than table order.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.11.33"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-b1200ce0596bb8d4cd9d","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.12.25","status":"rejected","reason":"Equal care among body members is broad solidarity; Eph 4:25 adds the precise truthful speech among mutually belonging members.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.12.25"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-47fac4d7c18713d8f43c","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.12.25","status":"rejected","reason":"This repeats the preceding equal-care proposal for the same verse; Eph 4:25 ties body membership to actual truth-telling.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.12.25"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-09c652f8935d98c02998","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.12.26","status":"rejected","reason":"Shared suffering in the body is genuine but does not address reciprocal counsel; Eccl 4:10 directly depicts one companion lifting another.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.12.26"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-99eb10efb78d43ecf9a8","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.12.26","status":"rejected","reason":"The duplicate body-suffering proposal adds no distinct exchange beyond the already selected companion-lifting scene in Eccl 4:10.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.12.26"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d552f08ebe90ea8611d9","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.13.4","status":"rejected","reason":"Love's patience and kindness are true but general; Prov 15:18 names patience's particular effect of quieting a quarrel.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.13.4"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-906275fc977ce844f84e","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.13.4","status":"rejected","reason":"This repeats the patient-love point without a specific dispute; Prov 15:18 states the social effect explicitly.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.13.4"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-bc0ba84323cea138afef","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.13.6","status":"rejected","reason":"Love rejoicing with truth is a valid association, but Eph 4:25 gives the more exact act of speaking truth to a fellow member.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.13.6"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-15bf9191c0c5530bd127","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.13.6","status":"rejected","reason":"The repeated truth-and-love proposal is broader than the selected Eph 4:25 reciprocal truth instruction.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.13.6"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-813af020f4046d8fe573","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.13.7","status":"rejected","reason":"Bearing all things is general endurance and does not show counsel or a quarrel resolved; Prov 15:18 is closer to paragraph 28.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.13.7"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-0c7a1c5566912190cf99","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.3.3","status":"rejected","reason":"The verse diagnoses jealousy and strife but lacks the lawsuit's explicit defeat and rival claims found in 1 Cor 6:6-7.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.3.3"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-6b07eaea29df4bf451ec","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.6.5","status":"rejected","reason":"The wise mediator is context for the accepted litigation passage; this verse adds no independent point to the selected lawsuit-and-loss annotation.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.6.5"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-97754a8915aac537c567","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.6.6","status":"accepted","reason":"The Greek explicitly says brother litigates against brother, matching paragraph 26's contested-right scene.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.6.6","SBLGNT:1Cor.6.7"],"annotations":["S103-INC-MTF-001"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-4f0a3197b3a18937d076","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.6.7","status":"accepted","reason":"The verse names intra-community lawsuits a defeat and proposes bearing wrong, a distinct remedy to the opening dispute; its link is a motif rather than a Qur'anic counter-narrative.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.6.6","SBLGNT:1Cor.6.7"],"annotations":["S103-INC-MTF-001"]}
