 {"connection_id":"BC-a9cba03144a4586c8fdf","ref":"SBLGNT:1John.4.21","status":"rejected","reason":"The command to love a brother continues 4:20's general love test; Lev 19:17-18 more closely connects love with corrective speech.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1John.4.21"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-757c8219d6e79b2bd750","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.3.11","status":"rejected","reason":"This restates Ps 34:15 in Greek and gives no dispute or repaired relationship; Matt 5:24 specifies reconciliation with an estranged brother.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.3.11"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-addee34ffb9c9a8b1ebc","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.3.11","status":"rejected","reason":"Peter's seek-and-pursue-peace wording is a direct echo of the psalm but lacks a concrete interparty scene; Matt 5:24 supplies one.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.3.11"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-95c6a74c810059cc463f","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.3.8","status":"rejected","reason":"The virtues are a general communal list; paragraph 26's more particular issue is how rival parties move from a right claim to peace.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.3.8"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-90916dcc9c688963b6da","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.3.8","status":"rejected","reason":"This repeats the general unity-and-brotherly-love list without a counsel or reconciliation action; Eph 2:14 offers the broken-wall image.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.3.8"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c30d8ac9cdf17e240c5c","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.3.9","status":"rejected","reason":"Blessing rather than returning abuse is a valid response to hostility, but Rom 12:20 gives the more specific enemy-feeding action paired with paragraph 28's needy-food image.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.3.9"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-6371e659c181db7b2725","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.4.8","status":"rejected","reason":"Love covering sins is a general forgiveness maxim; Prov 15:18 specifies patient conduct that quiets an active quarrel.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.4.8"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-22d950337ec5839ef499","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.4.8","status":"rejected","reason":"This repeats the love-covers-sins point; it says nothing about the reciprocal counsel or two groups at odds in this section.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.4.8"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-1c3fdd2fe3c77f09c85d","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.4.9","status":"rejected","reason":"Hospitality without complaint is concrete but concerns hosts and guests rather than mutual truth, legal contention or enemy reconciliation.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.4.9"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-dafe83ae4073bf4f8b87","ref":"SBLGNT:1Thess.5.11","status":"rejected","reason":"Mutual encouragement and building are close, but Heb 10:24-25 adds the surah's paired emphasis on good works and continued meeting; the Thessalonian verse would repeat that selected point.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Thess.5.11"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-fc146cbb75b41a7f1631","ref":"SBLGNT:1Thess.5.14","status":"rejected","reason":"Different care for disorderly, fainthearted and weak people is valuable, but the verse does not present reciprocal giving and receiving of truth; Heb 10:24-25 does.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Thess.5.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-a03657d158064158a0b9","ref":"SBLGNT:1Thess.5.14","status":"rejected","reason":"The repeated proposal emphasizes patience with all, yet lacks paragraph 28's actual quarrel; Prov 15:18 shows patience quieting one.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Thess.5.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-a5596daa3af4c5437696","ref":"SBLGNT:1Thess.5.15","status":"rejected","reason":"Seeking good rather than retaliation is general; Rom 12:20-21 spells out the material response to a hungry enemy in paragraph 28.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Thess.5.15"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-6d2162a2b2449a07dadd","ref":"SBLGNT:2Cor.13.11","status":"rejected","reason":"The closing list of restoration, agreement and peace states the same arc broadly; Matt 5:23-25 gives the concrete offended-brother and lawsuit scenes.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Cor.13.11"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-3d5595483d886ee5db50","ref":"SBLGNT:2Cor.2.7","status":"rejected","reason":"Forgiving a disciplined member is a specific church-discipline episode; paragraph 28's barış scenes concern opposed groups, spouses and enemies.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Cor.2.7"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-395e353dbc607180dfc5","ref":"SBLGNT:2Cor.2.8","status":"rejected","reason":"Reaffirming love continues 2:7's discipline episode, not the paragraph's dispute-resolution or enemy-care imagery.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Cor.2.8"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c78bf48daa57440514c0","ref":"SBLGNT:2Thess.3.15","status":"rejected","reason":"Admonishing a disobedient person as a brother is close but one-directional discipline; Lev 19:17-18 already joins correction to preserved kinship more directly.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Thess.3.15"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-32ede8a4f0b8dc82649a","ref":"SBLGNT:2Tim.2.23","status":"rejected","reason":"Avoiding foolish controversies is a teacher's rule; it does not test true rival claims or the mutuality of counsel in paragraph 27.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Tim.2.23"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-6b1f7e4e9c5eae576fc3","ref":"SBLGNT:2Tim.2.24","status":"rejected","reason":"The servant's gentleness and patience are one teacher's posture, whereas Prov 15:18 supplies the specific effect of patience on a quarrel.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Tim.2.24"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-ddd76771178f3e344164","ref":"SBLGNT:2Tim.2.24","status":"rejected","reason":"This repeats the nonquarrelsome teacher point and does not describe mutual advice among peers.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Tim.2.24"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-08d66d5ebfd7ea10617e","ref":"SBLGNT:2Tim.2.25","status":"rejected","reason":"Gentle correction of opponents is asymmetric teaching by the Lord's servant; Lev 19:17-18 gives the closer neighbor-to-neighbor duty.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Tim.2.25"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-07985eac141fd2b03308","ref":"SBLGNT:2Tim.2.25","status":"rejected","reason":"The second proposal correctly notes truth but repeats one-directional teacher correction, not the two-sided exchange stressed in paragraph 27.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Tim.2.25"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-5ea140dd58e76ca31801","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.15.2","status":"rejected","reason":"The circumcision dispute is concrete but concerns a different inclusion controversy whose council resolution does not depict reciprocal advice about truth and endurance.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.15.2"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-8217995db74e77a13f6d","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.15.28","status":"rejected","reason":"This verse reports the council's Spirit-and-us decision, not how opposed parties exchanged counsel; the proposed causal link to a mutual resolution exceeds the wording.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.15.28"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-986a29ad311cc013a9f1","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.15.39","status":"rejected","reason":"Paul and Barnabas separate after sharp disagreement, a useful limit, but not a Qur'anic counter-narrative; this episode does not state a general rival resolution for 103:3.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.15.39"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-34ac00d57b93a61407b4","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.4.32","status":"rejected","reason":"Common possessions and one heart show solidarity, but lack the text's contested right or exchange of truth; Eccl 4:10 gives direct mutual aid.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.4.32"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-66fedd1c1175b15f36be","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.4.32","status":"rejected","reason":"This duplicates the communal-possession point and does not portray the paragraph's reciprocal counsel.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.4.32"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d625fd9518cc7dd383ef","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.6.1","status":"rejected","reason":"The neglected widows identify a distribution dispute; the verse does not yet show its repair or mutual exhortation, so the proposed correspondence rests on another scene.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.6.1"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-46075658394ca3cc36ef","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.9.27","status":"rejected","reason":"Barnabas introduces Saul, but fear and acceptance are supplied by surrounding Acts 9:26-28, not the opened verse; this is mediation rather than the reciprocal practice of 103:3.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.9.27"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-f81950c792bd4311d935","ref":"SBLGNT:Col.3.13","status":"rejected","reason":"Mutual bearing and forgiving are apt but do not connect directly to truthful counsel or an enemy scene; Lev 19:17-18 covers correction and kinship together.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Col.3.13"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-2d42febd8ebc953bb86d","ref":"SBLGNT:Col.3.13","status":"rejected","reason":"The repeated forgiveness proposal gives a complaint setting, but paragraph 28's distinctive issue is active peacemaking across hostility; Matt 5:24 is closer.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Col.3.13"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-36435868d6249a49856a","ref":"SBLGNT:Col.3.14","status":"rejected","reason":"Love as a bond is a general metaphor; Eph 2:14 names hostility's dividing wall and its removal, closer to paragraph 26's estrangement.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Col.3.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-3ff0941336793076a3d1","ref":"SBLGNT:Col.3.14","status":"rejected","reason":"This repeats the love-as-bond proposal; it does not ground the Arabic asr lexical sense, and the Hebrew root investigation cautions against a lexical parallel.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Col.3.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-67c504eb566e4597b2f8","ref":"SBLGNT:Col.3.15","status":"rejected","reason":"The one-body peace image is genuine but less specific to two hostile groups than Eph 2:14-16.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Col.3.15"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-458df4fcd09387deb09a","ref":"SBLGNT:Col.3.15","status":"rejected","reason":"This duplicates one-body peace, without the explicit former hostility and barrier-removal of Eph 2:14-16.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Col.3.15"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-fbedc249b4a034bdfcde","ref":"SBLGNT:Col.3.16","status":"rejected","reason":"Teaching and admonishing one another is exact mutual instruction, but the verse concerns Christ's word in worship; Eph 4:25 and Heb 10:24-25 jointly add truth, good works and assembly with clearer paragraph fit.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Col.3.16"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-fc1c7a01fd7c5d77fe0d","ref":"SBLGNT:Eph.2.14","status":"accepted","reason":"Greek explicitly describes two parties made one and a hostile dividing wall removed, matching paragraph 26's estrangement image.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Eph.2.14","SBLGNT:Eph.2.16"],"annotations":["S103-INC-MTF-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-347d0c5417031e551aad","ref":"SBLGNT:Eph.2.14","status":"accepted","reason":"The same wall-and-hostility wording substantiates the proposed transformation, within the letter's distinct Christological framework.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Eph.2.14","SBLGNT:Eph.2.16"],"annotations":["S103-INC-MTF-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-e303d7e15284aff7dcf2","ref":"SBLGNT:Eph.2.16","status":"accepted","reason":"Verse 16 explicitly says both are reconciled in one body and hostility is killed, continuing 2:14's image.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Eph.2.14","SBLGNT:Eph.2.16"],"annotations":["S103-INC-MTF-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-15312f24745896d58a66","ref":"SBLGNT:Eph.4.15","status":"rejected","reason":"Truth in love is a close phrase but the verse does not itself specify a neighbor or reciprocal membership; 4:25 directly supplies both.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Eph.4.15"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d129b3a3779eb230e890","ref":"SBLGNT:Eph.4.15","status":"rejected","reason":"The duplicate truth-in-love proposal is less precise about the relation between speakers than Eph 4:25's each-to-neighbor instruction.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Eph.4.15"],"annotations":[]}
*** End Patch"));

