text(await tools.apply_patch("*** Begin Patch
*** Update File: /Volumes/aro/projects/prose_generation/enrichment/bible/work/s103/ehlikitap-images.sol.max.s103-20261009/sec9/verdicts.jsonl
@@
 {"connection_id":"BC-57362345d682a92f1980","ref":"WLC:Ezra.6.14","status":"rejected","reason":"Aramaic וּמַצְלְחִ֔ין means prospering in temple building; sound correspondence to ص ل ح does not establish reconciliation or righteous deeds.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["WLC:Ezra.6.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-034ff7f52d69d483451a","ref":"WLC:Gen.11.3","status":"rejected","reason":"Babel's reciprocal speech coordinates brickmaking; the verse itself does not call the project self-exalting, nor discuss truthful or patient counsel.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.11.3"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-3302c06b5fb82c0bf5fa","ref":"WLC:Gen.11.7","status":"rejected","reason":"Confused speech prevents mutual understanding at Babel, but this is divine dispersal of a building project rather than failed ethical exhortation.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.11.7"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-3f91fc1b98a35779f96b","ref":"WLC:Gen.13.8","status":"rejected","reason":"Abram rejects strife with Lot because they are kin, a real relational analogy; Matt 5:24 more explicitly requires repair after a grievance rather than asking quarrelling not begin.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.13.8"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-8555f1988bc58145e267","ref":"WLC:Gen.13.8","status":"rejected","reason":"This repeats Abram's brotherhood appeal to Lot; the verse asks to avoid a quarrel rather than depicting reciprocal counsel or reconciliation already achieved.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.13.8"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d7578273c32480b027f2","ref":"WLC:Gen.33.4","status":"rejected","reason":"Esau embraces Jacob, but this verse does not state Jacob's prior fear or a lasting resolution; the enemy-to-friend claim needs surrounding narrative and is less explicit than the selected ethical commands.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.33.4"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-13aa0e94d15b7329c278","ref":"WLC:Gen.33.4","status":"rejected","reason":"The repeated reunion scene shows a kiss and tears, not a spoken exchange of truth or patience; Exod 23:5 gives a direct act across enmity.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.33.4"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-f52ba1225b3cb0dc4f63","ref":"WLC:Gen.37.4","status":"rejected","reason":"Joseph's brothers cannot speak peaceably, a strong inverse speech image; Zech 8:16 supplies the positive instruction to speak truth and judge peace, closer to paragraph 27.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.37.4"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d97473cd8755e10388e7","ref":"WLC:Gen.4.9","status":"rejected","reason":"Cain's denial of being his brother's keeper is an opposite of responsibility, but it is narrative evasion after murder, not a rival teaching or general counter-narrative to 103:3.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.4.9"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-7f0f0bc14aa08d46c20d","ref":"WLC:Gen.45.15","status":"rejected","reason":"Joseph's brothers speak to him after kisses and tears, but the verse does not state what they say; it cannot attest mutual truth-counsel.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.45.15"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-66a7672dd31af29c9d5f","ref":"WLC:Gen.45.5","status":"rejected","reason":"Joseph reframes his sale as God's life-preserving purpose, a one-way reassurance after betrayal; it is not the surah's mutual exhortation to haqq and patience.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.45.5"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-20b1035bc2acd0585392","ref":"WLC:Gen.50.17","status":"rejected","reason":"The brothers ask Joseph's forgiveness and he weeps, but the verse does not show his reply or settled reconciliation; Matt 5:24 provides the direct repair command.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.50.17"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-b32cbbb2f19c897bd7b6","ref":"WLC:Gen.50.21","status":"rejected","reason":"Joseph comforts his fearful brothers and promises provision, but this is one family's narrated aftermath, not reciprocal instruction; Prov 25:21 states care for an enemy as a general command.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.50.21"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-9bdb2b5fa73431bb0a8e","ref":"WLC:Gen.50.21","status":"rejected","reason":"The duplicate Joseph scene has compassionate speech and material care, but no explicit former-enemy language or two-way counsel in this verse.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["WLC:Gen.50.21"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-42332aee8c1b2fa7c15e","ref":"WLC:Isa.1.13","status":"rejected","reason":"WLC וַעֲצָרָֽה is assembly paired with wrongdoing; the proposed ع ص ر sound match does not mean the Arabic page's affection or kinship.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["WLC:Isa.1.13"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-ceaa351fab67ef2adfed","ref":"WLC:Isa.1.17","status":"rejected","reason":"Learning good and defending orphan and widow are justice duties, but this verse lacks the mutual truth-speaking and peacemaking together found in Zech 8:16.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Isa.1.17"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-bc366737d30e8e00fabc","ref":"WLC:Isa.10.1","status":"accepted","reason":"The Hebrew root חקק explicitly forms unjust decrees, showing decree-making cannot by itself certify right; cognacy to Arabic ح ق ق remains sound-only.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["WLC:Prov.8.15","WLC:Isa.10.1"],"annotations":["S103-TEV-SYD-002"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-4bb2fe3f520b5f6661c8","ref":"WLC:Isa.19.25","status":"rejected","reason":"Egypt, Assyria and Israel share blessing here, but prior rivalry and its reconciliation require a larger oracle; this verse does not narrate interpersonal counsel.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["WLC:Isa.19.25"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-201af0fd6ea97bcfdaff","ref":"WLC:Isa.32.17","status":"rejected","reason":"The work of righteousness becomes peace and security, a broad formula; Jas 3:18 adds actual peacemakers and their peaceful sowing.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["WLC:Isa.32.17"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-a441e15314954d72b149","ref":"WLC:Isa.32.17","status":"rejected","reason":"This repeats righteousness producing peace; the verse has no opposed parties or counsel, unlike Zech 8:16's neighbor speech and peace judgment.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["WLC:Isa.32.17"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-b1238b60ae0ada4d5233","ref":"WLC:Isa.5.23","status":"rejected","reason":"Bribed judges vindicate the wicked and deprive the righteous, a legal corruption case; Prov 18:17 better addresses the opposing parties' own seeming right.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["WLC:Isa.5.23"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-9171ef62a80193d7fe86","ref":"WLC:Isa.51.12","status":"rejected","reason":"The Hebrew אֱנוֹשׁ is mortal and dies like grass, but Ps 8:5 gives a shorter cognate example; neither verse says social intimacy.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["WLC:Isa.51.12"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-a138904ba4819bf34250","ref":"WLC:Isa.58.10","status":"rejected","reason":"Satisfying the afflicted hungry person is direct charity, but the paragraph's distinct question is reciprocal counsel; Prov 25:21 adds enemy care to food aid.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Isa.58.10"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-ec24e873f695d48abdaf","ref":"WLC:Isa.58.7","status":"rejected","reason":"Bread sharing and not hiding from one's flesh unite charity and kinship, but the verse does not depict hostility repaired; Prov 25:21 expressly names the enemy.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["WLC:Isa.58.7"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-6e02269fb282c668bc22","ref":"WLC:Isa.58.9","status":"rejected","reason":"Removing the yoke, pointing finger and evil speech is a social-justice call; it lacks the specific right-and-peace judgment of Zech 8:16.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Isa.58.9"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-01f61c19e0f28e794481","ref":"WLC:Jer.12.1","status":"rejected","reason":"WLC צָלֵ֔חָה describes the wicked way prospering, a semantic warning against equating Hebrew צלח with righteous ṣāliḥ deeds or reconciliation.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["WLC:Jer.12.1"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-a960a86bc731a35b375a","ref":"WLC:Jer.31.34","status":"rejected","reason":"The new-covenant oracle says no one will teach neighbor to know YHWH because all will know him; it does not abolish all mutual moral counsel, so the proposed Qur'anic counter-narrative overgeneralizes.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Jer.31.34"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-6d4e64843a5486057d51","ref":"WLC:Jer.9.3","status":"rejected","reason":"In WLC numbering, 9:3 warns against brothers and neighbors, but the tongues trained in lies and lack of truth are in 9:4; the candidate assigns 9:4's wording to 9:3.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Jer.9.3"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-f81e8adc519b01abf137","ref":"WLC:Jer.9.4","status":"rejected","reason":"In WLC numbering, 9:4 says neighbors deceive and do not speak truth; the brother-supplanting and slander wording belongs to 9:3, so the candidate mislocates that claim.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Jer.9.4"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-05b9acdb027751bc46ba","ref":"WLC:Job.14.1","status":"rejected","reason":"The WLC verse begins אָדָם, not אֱנוֹשׁ or another אנש form; its mortal-trouble motif cannot serve as evidence for the proposed cognate here.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["WLC:Job.14.1"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c1f802985747d7a8de99","ref":"WLC:Job.14.1","status":"rejected","reason":"The repeated cognate claim fails at the cited verse: Job 14:1 uses אָדָם; Ps 8:5 supplies the actual אֱנוֹשׁ witness.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["WLC:Job.14.1"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-e8c0d2d9c6168c83ac74","ref":"WLC:Job.19.13","status":"rejected","reason":"Job's brothers and acquaintances are distant, a real inverse image, but it depicts suffered abandonment rather than rival claims or counsel repairing the bond.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["WLC:Job.19.13"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-7c6fa630dd4026adb80d","ref":"WLC:Job.19.19","status":"rejected","reason":"Job's confidants abhor him and loved ones turn against him, but no reconciliation follows in this verse; it is a lament rather than a counsel scene.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["WLC:Job.19.19"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-5cdd870b1d2fa61aa8d9","ref":"WLC:Job.19.19","status":"rejected","reason":"The duplicate friend-betrayal proposal contrasts with companionship, but the selected Eccl 4:10 shows the paragraph's positive helper-versus-isolation contrast.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Job.19.19"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-9df2a4860ead2fe38b83","ref":"WLC:Job.2.13","status":"rejected","reason":"Job's friends sit silently in grief, which is presence rather than mutual exhortation; Eccl 4:10 names one companion's active aid to another.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Job.2.13"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-db55d6303806b9b74570","ref":"WLC:Job.4.17","status":"rejected","reason":"אֱנוֹשׁ here is a mortal contrasted with God in a question about righteousness, not an intimate friend; Ps 8:5 states the lexical human sense without conflating the two.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["WLC:Job.4.17"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c0251bb596d8ab6ca48a","ref":"WLC:Job.42.10","status":"rejected","reason":"Job prays for friends after dispute, but this is a one-way act toward God and the verse's restoration is divine; it does not depict mutual counsel.","paragraphs":[28],"evidence":["WLC:Job.42.10"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-06758123117a0dffe8fa","ref":"WLC:Job.42.11","status":"rejected","reason":"Kin and former acquaintances eat with and comfort Job, but the verse describes later consolation, not the quarrel's resolution or reciprocal truth.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Job.42.11"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-08ccd83157d4e5e564f6","ref":"WLC:Job.6.14","status":"rejected","reason":"The compressed Hebrew requests ḥesed from a friend for one collapsing, but does not show the patient companion acting; Eccl 4:10 offers an explicit helping scene.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Job.6.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-e3d6974831fe5e24ec51","ref":"WLC:Joel.1.14","status":"rejected","reason":"The Hebrew עֲצָרָ֔ה is a called assembly during disaster; its sound match to Arabic ع ص ر does not carry the page's kinship or temporal sense.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["WLC:Joel.1.14"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-1e0979608848bcbce987","ref":"WLC:Lev.19.17","status":"accepted","reason":"The Hebrew explicitly joins no hatred of a brother with direct reproof of a fellow, preserving relationship through correction.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["WLC:Lev.19.17","WLC:Lev.19.18"],"annotations":["S103-TEV-MTF-002"]}
*** End Patch"));

