+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"WLC:Ps.55.21","status":"rejected","reason":"The former companion attacks those at peace and violates his covenant, confirming betrayal context but not the selected movement toward repair.","paragraphs":[26],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.55.21"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"SBLGNT:Luke.9.24","status":"accepted","reason":"Luke 9:24 sets the self-loss warning in Jesus-following and supports the annotation's stated contextual limit; Corpus Coranicum cites it for eschatological loss.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Luke.9.25","SBLGNT:Luke.9.24","CORPUSCORANICUM:103:2:anmerkung"],"annotations":["S103-INC-MTF-004"]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"SBLGNT:Luke.9.25","status":"accepted","reason":"The Greek asks what a human gains by winning the world yet losing himself, a close gain/loss image to 103:2 with a distinct Jesus-following setting.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Luke.9.25","SBLGNT:Luke.9.24","CORPUSCORANICUM:103:2:anmerkung"],"annotations":["S103-INC-MTF-004"]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"SBLGNT:Phil.3.7","status":"rejected","reason":"Paul revalues personal gains as loss for Christ, as the Corpus Coranicum note observes; paragraph 27's selected Luke text more directly names the human losing himself.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Phil.3.7"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"SBLGNT:Phil.3.8","status":"rejected","reason":"The continued accounting of everything as loss is Paul's Christological autobiography, not the surah's shared counsel and social peace.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Phil.3.8"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"SBLGNT:1Thess.4.18","status":"rejected","reason":"Greek παρακαλεῖτε ἀλλήλους is explicit mutual exhortation, but it refers to consoling one another about the dead; Heb 10:24-25 adds good works and common assembly to the section's concern.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Thess.4.18"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"CORPUSCORANICUM:103:2:anmerkung","status":"accepted","reason":"The local scholarly note specifically records Luke 9:24 as a comparison for eschatological loss; its Peshitta root claim remains unverified because that witness is not local.","paragraphs":[27],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Luke.9.25","SBLGNT:Luke.9.24","CORPUSCORANICUM:103:2:anmerkung"],"annotations":["S103-INC-MTF-004"]}
*** End Patch"));

